# Build trees
build/
build-*/
out/
cmake-build-*/

# FetchContent cache. Redirected here by FETCHCONTENT_BASE_DIR so downloads
# survive clean builds and can be shared across build directories.
external/

# vcpkg manifest-mode install tree
vcpkg_installed/

# Editors / tooling
.vs/
.vscode/
.idea/
.cache/
compile_commands.json

# Python
__pycache__/
*.egg-info/
.venv/
dist/
wheelhouse/

# Nuclear data. Raw ENDF tapes are large and regenerable via
# data/endf/fetch_endf.sh; the staged store is committed (see the negation).
data/endf/B-VIII.1/
*.h5
!data/nusift_b8.1.h5
!tests/data/*.h5

# Built Python extension, placed beside the sources so an in-tree build is importable. The
# DLLs are the Windows case of the same thing: an in-tree extension finds hdf5 and its
# dependencies next to itself. They are build output, not sources -- committing them put 4 MB
# of Windows binaries into every wheel, including the Linux and macOS ones, since
# wheel.packages ships this directory whole.
python/nusift/*.pyd
python/nusift/*.so
python/nusift/*.dll
python/nusift/*.dylib
python/nusift/data/

# Machine-local preset overrides (vcpkg root, compiler paths). Never committed.
CMakeUserPresets.json

# The review document is kept beside the tree, never in it.
CODE_REVIEW.md

# The branch review notes, same as CODE_REVIEW.md above.
BRANCH_REVIEW.md

# The capability roadmap, same as the two above: a working document that is reasoned over
# beside the tree rather than shipped with it.
CAPABILITY_PLANNING.md

# The publications the coefficients are read from: copyrighted documents, of which the tree
# carries the TABLES rather than the sources they were transcribed from -- each cited in
# validation/references/README.md the way every other published number here is cited, so anyone
# can check a transcription against their own copy.
#
# A pattern rather than a list of names. Naming them individually meant that the next one
# dropped into the root was not covered, and `git add -A` committed 700 KB of it before anyone
# noticed. No PDF at the top level belongs in this repository.
/*.pdf
